 the video but  it is true harry selden has seen that  the  empire will fall and that's predicted by  psycho history  his main goal is not to upset the order  but to minimize the suffering that's  coming  after things fall apart he wants to get  humanity back  on track quicker and establishes the  foundations to help accelerate the rise  of a new  empire later in the trailer we hear him  describe what's coming  he says order will vanish wars will be  endless  you can't save yourselves but you can  save your legacy  beyond the mention of legacy this is  pretty consistent with how things play  out in the books  the fall of the empire is supposed to  lead to 30 000 years of barbarism and  chaos  selden thinks he can shorten that to a  thousand years using psycho history  but no one understands it at this point  and there's no real motivation for the  people in power to listen to him  that's where galdornik comes in she's a  brilliant mathematician that harry hired  to help him work on psycho history  in the first trailer we saw her journey  from her home world and we saw her  meeting with selden for the first time  there's a couple more glimpses of that  here  in this trailer we see her looking at  the equations through the prime radian  and saying his calculations are correct  the empire is dying  so seldon has this situation where he  can see what's going to happen  no one really wants to listen to him no  one really understands what he's saying  and galdorna can actually understand the  math she's there to start working with  him  but still seems impartial since she  hasn't started yet  this all lends credence to her  professional opinion on the equations  where it looks like the tv show will  diverge from the source material  it looks like there's a lot more tension  in the empire  and possibly even some revolutionary  stuff going on  on trantor we hear gal tell the emperor  that  only the psycho historians can shorten  the darkness  and we hear the emperor say tha